Package: cnijfilter2
Version: 6.90-6loong64
Architecture: loong64
Maintainer: atree <local>
Depends: cups, libcups2t64 | libcups2, libcupsimage2t64 | libcupsimage2, libc6 (>= 2.17), libgcc-s1, libusb-1.0-0
Recommends: cups-filters, libxml2
Suggests: system-config-printer
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.canon.com
Description: Canon IJ Printer Driver for LoongArch64 (fully native)
 Canon IJ printer driver (cnijfilter2 6.90) rebuilt from source as 100%
 native LoongArch64 binaries. No emulation layer and no wrapper scripts
 are used anywhere in the package.
 .
 Provides the CUPS backend cnijbe2 (USB + network transport), the
 rastertocanonij / cmdtocanonij2 / cmdtocanonij3 filters, the cnijlgmon3
 ink-level / status monitor and PPD files for the PIXMA G3000 / G3010 /
 G3020 / G3060 / G3080 series and many other supported Canon inkjet
 models. Maintenance functions (cleaning, nozzle check, print head
 alignment) are driven through the CUPS command interface.
 .
 Both transports are verified on real hardware: print data is sent as
 IVEC over TCP 9100 (RAW), while status / control uses Canon's CHMP
 (HTTP management protocol: POST to submit, then GET to fetch the
 chunked response body). Printer discovery uses SNMP v1 with the Canon
 private MIB (enterprise 1602) over unicast.
 .
 The package installs its files in the Debian-common CUPS locations and,
 at post-install time, probes the CUPS directories that are actually
 active on the host (cups-config, then well-known fallbacks) and adds
 symlinks when they differ, so the same .deb also works on layouts such
 as /usr/lib64/cups or /usr/libexec/cups.
